sw/test/ - cgra CLI unit tests
==============================

    test_sw.c   assert.h unit tests for the DSL parser (dsl.c) and the mode
                compiler + engines (compile.c). Covers section/directive
                parsing, $variable expansion, parse-error rejection, the
                built-in defaults, diagonal mode_compile + cfg_decode, and the
                matvec/scan/conv engines vs. a host reference (run against the
                sim: emulator, so no FPGA). Two further groups guard the
                performance work: engine results must be identical on sim: and
                sim:v2 while costing strictly fewer round trips and bytes, and
                conv must actually skip its Toeplitz matrix's zero tiles
                (asserted as >4x fewer round trips than the equivalent dense
                matvec) rather than streaming them.
    kernel_cases.h
                shared scalar-reference workload: vector operations, DSL modes,
                dot, 5x7 matvec, scans and convolution, with signed overflow and
                19-element tails. Runs on eight geometries in v2 and v3 and is
                reused by hw/sim/gen_kernel_vectors.c for RTL replay.

CAREFUL when adding a check: CHECK() evaluates its condition exactly once, on
purpose -- see the note in lib/test/README.

TAP-style output; non-zero exit on failure.

Run from the repository root (make -C sw -f sw.mk <target>)
-------------------------------
    unit                 build + run the unit tests
    smoke                CLI smoke tests against the emulator
    test                 unit + smoke + CLI shell/Python regressions
    PROFILE=asan test    same, under AddressSanitizer + UBSan
    valgrind             unit tests under valgrind

Compiled -UNDEBUG so assert() fires in any PROFILE.
CLI regressions added after the September 2026 audit:
    test_cli.sh checks malformed/discovered configs, pipeline arity, numeric
    options, output preservation (including hard links) and write failures.
    It uses temporary files and sim:, and runs as part of make test.

test_sw.c also checks actual stdlib negation, swapped ALU sources on multiple
geometries/protocols, shared immediates, parser rollback, and engine argument
validation before device commands. See ../../TASKS.md for remaining work.

    test_bench.py uses Python 3's JSON parser, multiple v2/v3 geometries and
    a fake PTY device returning checksum-valid wrong data. Covers benchmark
    failure/skip accounting, scalar comparison, UTF-8/escaping, failure artifacts,
    strict CLI numbers, large search lists, file capacity and embedded NUL.
    Runs from sw/ as part of make test; needs Python 3 standard library only.

Strict parser tests cover transaction rollback for invalid/oversized fields,
section syntax, variable capacity/expansion, PE coordinates and output taps.

Pattern and reset regressions in test_sw.c reject inapplicable fields before
configuration/execution and check stateful ACC mappings with nonzero initial
registers, repeated calls, once/each/default policies and untouched NOP cells.
Both v2 and v3 run on 1x1, 2x3 and 3x2 meshes. Diagonals with too few steps
exercise routing state across chunks, followed by an explicit zero-step run.

    test_install.py copies the working sources to a temporary directory and
    builds/installs them there. Checks include lookup before init, stdlib copy
    content, a prefix with spaces/quote/ampersand, changing PREFIX without a
    clean, DESTDIR deployment, copy failures, and an external C client using
    the installed header/library/pkg-config. All CLI runs are outside the
    checkout, with isolated user configuration. No system install or FPGA.
    Run `make test-install` from the repository root; needs GNU make, a C11
    compiler/toolchain, Python 3, makeinfo and pkg-config. Also runs in Linux CI.
